{"created": "2025-11-04T19:55:45.075053+00:00", "modified": "2025-11-04T19:55:47.336170+00:00", "id": 17526619, "conceptrecid": "17526618", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.17526619", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.17526618", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.17526619", "metadata": {"title": "Neutrinos: The Lie of Light According to Luminodynamic Gravitation Theory", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.17526619", "publication_date": "2025-11-04", "description": "<div>\n<div>\n<div>\n<p>We present a radical reinterpretation of neutrinos within the frame- work of Luminodynamic Gravitation Theory (TGL), a unified field theory that derives gravity, quantum mechanics, and consciousness from a single photonic-informational substrate. We propose that neu- trinos are not fundamental particles but rather temporal remnants of photons&mdash;&ldquo;ex-light&ldquo; or &ldquo;light that was.&ldquo; This hypothesis, termed the Lie of Light, resolves multiple empirical anomalies: near-zero mass, ultra-weak interaction, flavor oscillation, and the cosmological neu- trino background. We demonstrate that &nu; = lim\u2206t&rarr;&infin; &gamma;(t&minus;\u2206t), where neutrinos emerge as temporally degraded photon states. Testable pre- dictions include temporal correlations between photon emission his- tory and contemporary neutrino flux, age-dependent neutrino decay signatures, and reinterpretation of oscillation as temporal phase evo- lution. If validated, this framework reduces the particle zoo, unifies electromagnetic and weak phenomena temporally, and positions TGL as the first empirically grounded unified theory of the 21st century.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Rotoli Miguel, Luiz Antonio", "affiliation": "Pontif\u00edcia Universidade Cat\u00f3lica de S\u00e3o Paulo"}], "keywords": ["Luminodynamic Gravitation", "Unified Field Theory", "Temporal Light", "Quantum Measurement", "Graviton Operator"], "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-nc-nd-4.0"}, "communities": [{"id": "luminodynamic-gravitation"}], "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "17526618"}}]}}, "title": "Neutrinos: The Lie of Light According to Luminodynamic Gravitation Theory", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/17526619", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/17526619", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/17526619?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.17526619", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.17526619", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.17526619", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/17526619/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/17526618", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/17526618", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.17526618", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.17526618", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:17526619/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:17526619/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/17526619/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/17526619/media-files", "thumbnails": {"10": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:17526619:lie_of_light.pdf/full/%5E10,/0/default.jpg", "50": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:17526619:lie_of_light.pdf/full/%5E50,/0/default.jpg", "100": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:17526619:lie_of_light.pdf/full/%5E100,/0/default.jpg", "250": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:17526619:lie_of_light.pdf/full/%5E250,/0/default.jpg", "750": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:17526619:lie_of_light.pdf/full/%5E750,/0/default.jpg", "1200": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:17526619:lie_of_light.pdf/full/%5E1200,/0/default.jpg"}, "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/17526619/versions/latest", "latest_html": "https://zenodo.o